      "writtenOn": "2023-11-03T04:37:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, they _are_ actually page aligned. The range marks the beginning of the first and last pages used by the buffer. As it is seen by the call in line 587:\n```\nret \u003d binder_get_page_range(alloc, buffer-\u003euser_data \u0026 PAGE_MASK,\n\t\t\t    PAGE_ALIGN(buffer-\u003euser_data + size));\n```\n\nThis is not so terrible as it\u0027s easy to calculate the inclusive range. It is the exclusive calculation of the final page in `has_page_addr` that took me a long time to figure out.\n\nI can also work on making this easier to digest for future readers.",
      "parentUuid": "aaf6da74_aba8a61a",
      "revId": "cba0dd82a60df879b05f8887eacf6faf78ab002b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
