        "id": 1069543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-03T17:13:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Yes, they are actually page aligned.\n\nIf buffers are page-aligned at head and tail, then why would there be any page sharing? I understand that we are forcing alignment to find all of the pages - but the point is that sharing occurs only because the buffers themselves are not page aligned (since that would mean that a 1-byte payload would require a whole page which would be wasteful)",
      "parentUuid": "99ab0856_64ffc969",
      "revId": "cba0dd82a60df879b05f8887eacf6faf78ab002b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
